## 6. Compliance

| ID | Requirement | Testable Criterion | Status (2026-07-07, Pass 1) |
|----|-------------|-------------------|------------------------------|
| CXC-HW-C1 | Headless model | A `.compose.yaml` widget with no render publishes/subscribes namespaces and runs on the headless runtime | PASS — test_headless_widgets.py C1; app.canvas is None throughout |
| CXC-HW-C2 | Jump-drive sim | fuel_tank + fuel_pump + jump_engine, headless, produce `jumpdrive/readiness` from fuel+charge with no Python and no ESP32 | PARTIAL — readiness = fuel≥40 AND charge≥60 works declaratively (triad tests); the ARITHMETIC residue (variable-rate drain, pump rate math) is the harvested DSL gap set, deferred to Pass 2 |
| CXC-HW-C3 | Continuous | A continuous widget updates its output every engine tick | PASS — 11 publishes over ticks 0.0..1.0 @10 Hz |
| CXC-HW-C4 | Periodic | A periodic widget fires only on its declared interval | PASS — nothing before interval; fires at k·interval |
| CXC-HW-C5 | Bus-triggered | A bus-triggered widget executes only when its trigger namespace/pattern publishes | PASS — exact + trailing-glob triggers; unrelated publishes don't wake it; t = arrival time |
| CXC-HW-C6 | Decoupling | The same headless logic runs on the hub; binding a physical sensor to its input namespace requires no change to the logic | PASS — external-publisher test + MQTT smoke (remote peer drives pump/damaged) |
| CXC-HW-C7 | Node-RED interop | A headless widget's emitted namespace is consumed by a Node-RED flow over MQTT, and vice versa | DEFERRED (out of Pass-1 scope); the MQTT leg it rides on is proven by the smoke |
| CXC-HW-C8 | No inline code | Headless logic uses declarative behaviors + the (future) restricted DSL; arbitrary code is refused ([CXC-BIND-BOUNDARY]) | PASS (refusal) — code fields stripped, expression maps refused in headless configs; DSL half deferred with C2 |
| CXC-HW-C9 | One tick, three clocks | A single `tick(t)` primitive is driven by continuous (10 Hz) / periodic / bus-triggered clock sources; no separate execution path per mode ([CXC-HW-RUNTIME]) | PASS — spy on RenderApp.tick catches every mode's execution |
| CXC-HW-C10 | Deterministic tick | `tick(t)` reads no wall-clock; `tick(0.0), tick(0.1)…` reproduces the exact output sequence in a golden test | PASS — identical drive ⇒ identical sequence (scheduler + direct-tick goldens) |
| CXC-HW-C11 | Roster deploy | The runtime fetches `bus://assets/headless/<runtime_id>.roster.yaml` + named widget configs from bus_storage; a local-file loader backs the same contract for goldens ([CXC-HW-DEPLOY]) | PASS — loader-parity test; triad live-deployed via bus_storage :8420 |
| CXC-HW-C12 | Bus seam | The same widget runs against an in-process bus and MQTT :1883 with zero widget changes | PASS — in-suite (two buses, identical sequences) + smoke_headless_mqtt.py 5/5 vs mqtt-broker.local |

